{
  "key": "letter-175-part-02",
  "number": 175,
  "generationId": "01a1e8e6-13a2-7b85-a028-a5146c5674b4",
  "voice": "Views",
  "speed": 0.9,
  "clips": [
    {
      "index": 10,
      "text": "The identification with life creates the gap.",
      "path": "audio/1971-175/11.mp3",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.889796
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "text": "And death has nothing to do with the future, it is always here and now.",
      "path": "audio/1971-175/12.mp3",
      "start": 4.126009,
      "end": 8.834330999999999
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "text": "Every moment, it is.",
      "path": "audio/1971-175/13.mp3",
      "start": 10.131406,
      "end": 12.056189999999999
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "text": "And when one ceases to regard it as something outside oneself and, so to speak, draws it into his consciousness and assimilates the idea of it, one is completely changed.",
      "path": "audio/1971-175/14.mp3",
      "start": 13.295465,
      "end": 24.802676
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "text": "He is in all truth born again.",
      "path": "audio/1971-175/15.mp3",
      "start": 26.528140999999998,
      "end": 28.922177
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "text": "And then there is no fear because then there is no gap.",
      "path": "audio/1971-175/16.mp3",
      "start": 30.797143,
      "end": 34.69
    }
  ]
}
